      "message": "Put the new front page up, as designed, in cobalt\n\nThe front page is the one designed for it, ported whole: the same words,\nsizes, motion and both themes, with its orange turned into the product's\ncobalt. It lives as front.html, front.css and front.js beside the app's\nown sheet, generated from the design export by a private script so the\nnext design change is a re-run rather than a rewrite. Nothing on it is\ncounted from this forge any more; everything on it is a story.\n\nThe forge's policy did not move to make room for it. The design's inline\nstyles became classes, its Google-hosted faces became two more bundled\nfonts (Bricolage Grotesque and Geist, both under the Open Font License,\ntheir texts beside them), its runtime became a small script of class\ntoggles, and its five tool marks became inline paths. The waitlist form\nposts where it always did and asks what the address is for, as the\nquestions on the page promise; the theme button posts the theme the page\nis not in.\n\nChange-Id: Ifront0173\nTask: t-3s27ja1v3nv1j81whb6v745vkm\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
